# Unified `entire explain` output format — Implementation Plan

> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (if subagents available) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.

**Goal:** Bring the brand-shaped output format introduced by PR #1078 to every other surface of `entire explain` (no-summary, temporary, list, session, failures, success), and replace the unhelpful `(no prompt)` fallback with a useful cascade.

**Architecture:** Add a small set of package-private helpers on `statusStyles` (identity / success / failure bullets, metadata rows, render wrappers) plus a single body renderer that routes through `defaultRenderTerminalMarkdown`. Each `entire explain` output path is rewritten to call those helpers; no new files. Failure paths write the styled block to `errW` and return `*SilentError` so `main.go` doesn't double-print.

**Tech Stack:** Go 1.26, lipgloss, glamour (existing brand renderer in `dispatch_tui.go`), cobra. No new dependencies.

**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-30-explain-unified-format-design.md`

**Pre-flight:**
- This plan executes inside the existing worktree `format-entire-explain`. The branch already contains PR #1078's changes (e008cc705 merged from origin/main).
- Per user preference, design/plan docs in `docs/superpowers/` are **not** committed.
- Code commits in this plan should be made (the no-commit rule applies only to planning docs under `docs/superpowers/`).
- Every code commit message must end with the `Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>` trailer (per CLAUDE.md commit conventions).

**Verification before any push:** `mise run fmt && mise run lint && mise run test:ci`. The full canary (`mise run test:e2e:canary`) is part of `test:ci`. Do **not** run `mise run test:e2e` — those are real-API tests that cost money.

---

## File Structure

| File | Change | Responsibility |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `cmd/entire/cli/status_style.go` | Modify | Add `explainRow` type + `identityBullet`, `successBullet`, `failureBullet`, `metadataRow`, `metadataRows`, `renderIdentity`, `renderSuccess`, `renderFailure` methods. ~80 net lines. |
| `cmd/entire/cli/status_style_test.go` | Modify | Unit tests for each new helper (color + NO_COLOR cases). |
| `cmd/entire/cli/explain.go` | Modify | Add `extractIntent`, `buildNoSummaryMarkdown`, `renderExplainBody` helpers. Rewrite no-summary branch of `formatCheckpointOutput`, body of `explainTemporaryCheckpoint`, `formatBranchCheckpoints`, `formatCheckpointGroup`, `formatSessionInfo`, `printNoTrailerMessage`, ambiguous-prefix rendering. Refactor `formatCheckpointSummaryError` to return `(label, rows, error)`. |
| `cmd/entire/cli/explain_test.go` | Modify | Update existing assertions (`Outcome:`, `Strategy:`, `Source Ref:`, `(no prompt)`, `No associated Entire checkpoint\n`). Add NO_COLOR cases per surface. Add intent-fallback test. Add no-double-print test. |
| `cmd/entire/cli/explain_summary_provider.go` | Modify | Replace `formatSummaryProviderDetails(p) string` with `summaryProviderRows(p) []explainRow`. |
| `cmd/entire/cli/explain_summary_provider_test.go` | Modify | Update assertions for new return shape. |
| `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/explain_test.go` | Modify | Update `"No associated Entire checkpoint"` assertion(s) to new failure shape. |
| `e2e/tests/explain_test.go` | Audit | Confirm no legacy substrings; PR #1078 already updated this file. |

No new files. No new packages. No exported API surface changes outside this package.

---

